          {
            "x": 2.178649237472767,
            "y": 12.910611231371064,
            "width": 92.73743016759778,
            "height": 86.09271523178808,
            "action": {
              "library": "H5P.AdvancedText 1.1",
              "params": {
                "text": "<p><strong>Livius' Legacy</strong><br>\nThe influence of Livius' writings extended beyond his lifetime. Throughout the centuries, his accounts have been a cornerstone for understanding Rome's early history and political culture. Medieval and Renaissance historians drew heavily from his work, and his impact on historical writing endures even into the modern era.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Critical Reception Over Time</strong><br>\nLivius' historiography has been subject to varying interpretations and criticisms over time. Some have questioned the accuracy of his accounts, pointing to his use of myth and legend, and his occasional errors in chronology. However, his detailed descriptions and engaging storytelling have earned him lasting respect.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Modern Relevance of Livius</strong><br>\nToday, scholars and educators continue to value Livius for his narrative history that provides insight not only into the events of the past but also into the values and ethos of ancient Rome. His works are still used as educational texts, offering a window into how Romans viewed their own history and civilization.</p>\n"
              },
              "metadata": {
                "contentType": "Text",
                "license": "U",
                "title": "Unbenannt: Text",
                "defaultLanguage": "en"
